## Done (this arc)
- **pkg P4b remote-registry TRANSPORT — SHIPPED + green** (prism-bigraph 96 suite + 43 lib
  + 6 new). The registry is a **CRDT of theories made literal**: a grow-only `map[name →
  map[version → Const<package>]]`, gated by `mesh_safety` (the closure-invariant PROOF, not
  a slogan) — the **keyed projection** of the mesh's full-state gossip. *Reuse not clone:*
  extracted `protocols/http.rs` (ONE `HttpServer` accept-loop door; refactored `rest_server`
  onto it) + built `protocols/registry.rs` (`RegistryServer` + `versions`/`fetch`/`publish` +
  a deterministic FNV `checksum`) on it — same door, same boundary byte-codec, same `algebra`
  join. Two registries `merge`-converge with no coordinator (`tests/registry_transport.rs`).
  pkg owns `RemoteRegistry` (chrysalis); seam in `to_pkg`. [[mesh_as_protocol]]
- **mesh M1 ladder COMPLETE:** closure invariant → `mesh:` protocol → live bridge →
  `.ys` surface+gate → runtime → distributed → N-peer → continuous gossip → SWIM
  (auto-discovery + failure detection) → `LiveField`.
